Add jq 1.8.2 and a windows_arm64 platform

jq has published jq-windows-arm64.exe since 1.8.0 (jqlang/jq#3340), but
the toolchain still pins 1.7 and offers no Windows arm64 platform, so
resolution fails outright on that host.

Adds the 1.8.2 hashes, a windows_arm64 entry, and moves the default to
1.8.2, which is the first version carrying every platform listed here.

Integrity values were computed from the released binaries and match the
sha256sum.txt published alongside them.

Pinning 1.7 explicitly on Windows arm64 still fails, because that release
has no such binary.

diff --git a/jq/toolchain/platforms.bzl b/jq/toolchain/platforms.bzl
index 0d979bc..ea9ff82 100644
--- a/jq/toolchain/platforms.bzl
+++ b/jq/toolchain/platforms.bzl
@@ -46,6 +46,13 @@ JQ_PLATFORMS = {
             "@platforms//cpu:x86_64",
         ],
     ),
+    "windows_arm64": struct(
+        release_platform = "windows-arm64",
+        compatible_with = [
+            "@platforms//os:windows",
+            "@platforms//cpu:arm64",
+        ],
+    ),
 }
 
 def _jq_platform_repo_impl(rctx):
diff --git a/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl b/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
index 4db2a91..f62ea18 100644
--- a/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
+++ b/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ load(":platforms.bzl", "JQ_PLATFORMS")
 
 TOOLCHAIN_TYPE = "@jq.bzl//jq/toolchain:type"
 DEFAULT_JQ_REPOSITORY = "jq"
-DEFAULT_JQ_VERSION = "1.7"
+DEFAULT_JQ_VERSION = "1.8.2"
 
 JqInfo = provider(
     doc = "Provide info for executing jq",
